floatstore_x86_64_O2.o, floatstore_a64_O2.o -- the x86-64 and AArch64 halves of
tests/stages/kuna-floatstore.xml.

What they are
  floatstore.c (beside them) compiled to relocatable objects. mat_param stores
  the 1.0f constants as integer bit patterns (movl $0x3f800000 / str w8) and the
  computed float with a float store (movss %xmm0,8(%rdi) / str s0,[x0,#8]), so
  the pointer's pointee is unknown bytes and the float store must print as a
  float store, not as an assignment C converts numerically.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu clang version 14.0.0-1ubuntu1.1:

      clang-14 -O2 -c floatstore.c -o floatstore_x86_64_O2.o
      clang-14 --target=aarch64-linux-gnu -O2 -c floatstore.c -o floatstore_a64_O2.o

  Prebuilt so the test does not depend on the host compiler's code generation.

  sha256
